    {
      "kind": "markdown",
      "text": "*Author: Byron*\n\n*Subject: outline I/O facilities for the application*"
    },
    {
      "kind": "context",
      "context_id": "context:namespace:trifecta.io:1"
    },
    {
      "kind": "markdown",
      "text": "`namespace trifecta.io`"
    },
    {
      "kind": "context",
      "context_id": "context:class:ComponentLog:1"
    },
    {
      "kind": "markdown",
      "text": "## ComponentLog\n\n### Data Structure"
    },
    {
      "kind": "type",
      "type_id": "type:trifecta.io.ComponentLog"
    },
    {
      "kind": "type",
      "type_id": "type:trifecta.io.LifespanToken"
    },
    {
      "kind": "context",
      "context_id": "context:class:FileLogSink:1"
    },
    {
      "kind": "markdown",
      "text": "## FileLogSink\n\n### Data Structure\n\n- class FileLog : ITextLogSink\n  - composition\n    - System.IO.StreamWriter Sink\n\n## Prompt\n\nA console interface for the user to query state and issue commands.\n\n## CommandParser\n\nLoads a sequence of commands from a structured file (e.g., JSON). Each command indicates a delay since the last\ncommand, an action to take, and an optional tag string. Commands simulate manual oversight and administration of\nthe factory and are routed to static singletons (e.g., actor.Directory.instance()._____()).\n\n## Interfaces"
    },
    {
      "kind": "type",
      "type_id": "type:trifecta.io.ITextLog"
    },
    {
      "kind": "type",
      "type_id": "type:trifecta.io.ITextLogSink"
    },
    {
      "kind": "markdown",
      "text": "## Diagrams"
    },
    {
      "kind": "diagram",
      "diagram_index": 0
    }
  ],
